  {
   "label": "Day 7",
   "date": "Sun, Jul 16",
   "title": "Finse — a day off the bikes",
   "prose": [
    "Getting to Finse: there is no road, so it’s the train. Leave the bikes in the Fretheim Hotel parking lot, check the bags at the hotel and pack lunch boxes. Take the 8:22 am Flåm Railway from Flåm station, right by the hotel, up the valley to Myrdal, then change to the Bergen Railway heading east over the mountains to Finse station. It takes about 2 hours 12 minutes in all.",
    "The hike: an easy hour and a half from Finse to Appelsinhytta, then about two hours up through Danskeskaret to the summit. It is steep for the first ten minutes or so, then crosses old snowfields (not glacier) with a close look at the Blue Ice."
   ],
